<xi:include href="./exercises.d/compute-dets.ptx" />

<exercise>
	<title>Counterintuitive determinant examples</title>
	<p>
		Provide example matrices with the requested properties.
		<ol>
			<li>
				A <m>2 \times 2</m> matrix <m>M</m>,
				the entries of which are <em>all</em> <alert>non</alert>zero,
				but for which <m>\det M = 0</m>.
			</li>
			<li> A nonzero <m>3 \times 3</m> upper triangular matrix <m>U</m> for which <m>\det U = 0</m>. </li>
			<li> A nonzero <m>3 \times 3</m> diagonal matrix <m>D</m> for which <m>\det D = 0</m>. </li>
			<li>
				A pair of <m>2 \times 2</m> matrices <m>A</m> and <m>B</m> for which both <m>\det A = 0</m> and <m>\det B = 0</m> but <m>\det (A + B) \neq 0</m>.
				(This demonstrates that <m>\det (A + B)</m> is <em>not</em> equal to <m>\det A + \det B</m> in general.)
			</li>
		</ol>
	</p>
</exercise>

